{"id":"HI-other-1","technology":"solar","policy_type":"other","who_decides":"local_government","state_body":null,"threshold_mw":null,"summary":"Solar facilities may not be built on agricultural-district land with the best (class A) soils, and on class B or C soils they are limited to 10 percent of the parcel or 20 acres, whichever is less, unless a county special permit is granted (with Land Use Commission approval over 15 acres) and the area is offered for farming at reduced rent and bonded for decommissioning. Wind facilities are a permitted use in the agricultural district if compatible with agriculture.","statute_citation":"Haw. Rev. Stat. 205-2(d)(6), 205-4.5(a)(20),(21)","statute_url":"https://data.capitol.hawaii.gov/hrscurrent/Vol04_Ch0201-0257/HRS0205/HRS_0205-0004_0005.htm","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"},
{"id":"HI-siting_authority-1","technology":"solar;wind","policy_type":"siting_authority","who_decides":"local_government","state_body":null,"threshold_mw":null,"summary":"Counties decide siting of wind and solar through zoning and county planning commission special permits; there is no state siting board. The state Land Use Commission must also approve a special permit for land over 15 acres in the agricultural district.","statute_citation":"Haw. Rev. Stat. 205-2(d), 205-4.5(a)(15),(20),(21), 205-6","statute_url":"https://data.capitol.hawaii.gov/hrscurrent/Vol04_Ch0201-0257/HRS0205/HRS_0205-0006.htm","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"}
